artifact.self_contained_problem:
A ring $B$ is called semi-graded (SG) if there is a family $\{B_n\}_{n\ge 0}$ of additive subgroups such that $B = \bigoplus_{n\ge 0} B_n$ as abelian groups, $1 \in B_0$, and $B_m B_n \subseteq B_0 \oplus B_1 \oplus \cdots \oplus B_{m+n}$ for all $m,n \ge 0$. Assume that $B$ satisfies the following conditions:
(C1) $B$ is left noetherian;
(C2) $B_0$ is left noetherian;
(C3) each $B_n$ is a finitely generated left $B_0$-module;
(C4) $B_0 \subseteq Z(B)$, the center of $B$.

Let $\mathrm{Gr}\text{-}B$ denote the category of $\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$-filtered (semi-graded) left $B$-modules with the natural notion of morphisms, let $\mathrm{tors}\text{-}B$ be its full subcategory of modules that are direct limits of modules with bounded grading (torsion modules), and let $\mathrm{qgr}\text{-}B$ be the quotient category $\mathrm{Gr}\text{-}B / \mathrm{tors}\text{-}B$, with canonical projection $\pi : \mathrm{Gr}\text{-}B \to \mathrm{qgr}\text{-}B$. For an object $\mathcal{M}$ of $\mathrm{qgr}\text{-}B$, define the section functor $\Gamma(\mathcal{M}) := \bigoplus_{n\ge 0} \mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{qgr}\text{-}B}(\pi(B), \mathcal{M}(n))$, where $(n)$ denotes the appropriate shift, and let $\Gamma(\pi(B))_{\ge 0}$ denote the non-negative part of $\Gamma(\pi(B))$.

Suppose further that $B$ satisfies the $\chi_1$ condition: $\mathrm{Ext}^1_B(B/B_{\ge 1}, M)$ is a finitely generated left $B_0$-module for every finitely generated semi-graded left $B$-module $M$.

Question: Does there exist an equivalence of categories
$$\mathrm{qgr}\text{-}B \;\simeq\; \mathrm{qgr}\text{-}\Gamma(\pi(B))_{\ge 0}\,?$$

